Fix real upstream build bugs (not AXOS features): the prebuilt GT-AX6000
rc/prebuild/GT-AX6000/hostapd_config_6e.o — linked into `rc` unconditionally
as of 0004-gt-ax6000-hostapd-config-6e-hostapd-decoupling.patch, since core
WLAN code (services.c's apply_config_to_driver()) needs it regardless of
RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD — itself needs several helper symbols that are, in
turn, gated behind CONFIG_HOSTAPD or RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD one level further
down. Confirmed via a real build attempt after 0004: `make gt-ax6000` still
fails linking `rc`, with "undefined reference to `wl_ascii_str_to_hex_str'"
and, separately, `bytes_to_hex`/`dm_unregister_app_restart_info` (all three
confirmed needed by hostapd_config_6e.o via `nm`, cross-checked against
every symbol every GT-AX6000 prebuilt object defines).

- common_utils.o (shared/Makefile, providing bytes_to_hex and
  dm_unregister_app_restart_info among others): has no internal
  CONFIG_HOSTAPD logic of its own (a plain utility file), but its inclusion
  in `shared`'s OBJS was gated on RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD — the same
  "downstream helper coupled to the feature flag, when the actual code that
  needs it is unconditional" shape as 0003's sys_util/gen_util and 0004's
  hostapd_config_6e.o fixes. Dropped that gate.

- wl_ascii_str_to_hex_str: normally declared/defined in shared/wlif_utils.c
  under CONFIG_HOSTAPD. First attempt was to duplicate it there under a
  matching `#ifndef CONFIG_HOSTAPD` — but that didn't fix the link failure,
  because shared/wlif_utils.c (and its wlif_utils_ax.c sibling) turn out to
  be compiled at all only when CONFIG_BCMWL5 is "y" (see shared/Makefile) —
  an older, non-AX driver generation flag that's off for this HND_ROUTER_AX
  chip, so neither file is ever built here regardless of CONFIG_HOSTAPD.
  Moved the actual definition into shared/common_utils.c instead (a
  verbatim copy of the CONFIG_HOSTAPD-gated version), since that file
  genuinely is always compiled (per the fix above). Kept a declaration in
  wlif_utils.h too, under the same `#ifndef CONFIG_HOSTAPD`, purely so any
  other translation unit that includes that header still sees a matching
  prototype.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0005. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

